<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Da Nang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tourane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Da Nang is a port city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, on a sheltered bay south of the Hai Van Pass. A French and Spanish fleet attacked it in 1858, the opening of the French conquest, and in 1888 the Nguyen court ceded it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as a concession. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a> it was a major American air and naval base.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/da-nang.jpg" alt="Da Nang" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Somerset999 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dragon_Bridge,_Da_Nang_during_day_-_20230819_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
